ption is of course shigaraki who's  in jakku and if we switch over to a  different part of the city Deku bakugou  and shotar injaku as well unlike  endeavor's group their main job isn't to  capture garaki or fight off any of the  nomu but rather their main priority is  helping with the evacuation meanwhile on  the streets the hero's sliding go was  arrested for being a traitor and this  was expected because Hawks are known for  a while that this guy was working for  the Liberation Army back inside the  hospital Endeavor and the Gang then  March in to confront garaki with the  doctor [ __ ] himself once he sees the  number one hero the anime then briefly  flashes over to a completely anime  original scene that takes place outside  natsuo's house in which fumi tells him  that she received a call from their dad  basically what happened is that endeavor  called her up to say that he wouldn't be  able to speak to them for a while  because of work and they both quickly  realized that something big must be  going on that sewer remarks that he  hopes things don't turn out like he did  in their Pro Hero walk because despite  Endeavor winning the bastard in the end  he did have a very hard time not dying  switching back to the hospital again as  garaki tries to run izawa easily trips  him up with The Binding cloth and uses  Erasure to reveal that old man does  actually have a quirk on the government  registry the doctor was officially  listed as being quarkless but here we  can see that he instantly aged up when  hit by Erasure indicating that his true  power is one that slows down the aging  process once it got erased by a Tsar his  true appearance was revealed to everyone  and in the mangere was confirmed later  on that he's at least 120 years old as  garaki then struggles to crawl away  detective tsukiuchi speculates that this  anti-asian Quirk is the same one wolf  once been using to survive since the  first generation this is a solid Theory  considering that the villains have  demonstrated the potential to replicate  quirks such as the Supreme generation  that seems to be possessed by every  black nomu In This Moment present Mike  then slaps the doctor's revenge for what  he did to shirakumo and while  questioning him some of the other Pro  Heroes start to evacuate the hospital  while one small piece of trivia is that  this guy here is takashita otherwise  known as the hero who used to go to  school with gentle criminal as we saw in  gentle's backstory the two of them used  to be in the same class but as they got  older takashita completely forgot who  gentle was triggering him so badly that  he became a villain so that his name  could be remembered by Future  Generations in any case with isawa  capturing garaki the animator takes us  to Police Headquarters which is acting  like a control center to coordinate this  whole operation this scene is another  anime original moment and it's these  police officers who mention what maker  is up to the impatient number five hero  surged ahead of everyone else to enter  the hospital morgue which is the only  way to access garaki's secret area  leaping through the hallway like a  rabbit she's then confronted by a horde  of mid-level nomu and this is when we  get the big reveal of the episode as it  turns out the Dr garaki they arrested  was actually a clone made from twice's  Quirk and the real version of the doctor  has been inside his secret lab the  entire time although it wasn't  explicitly made clear in the anime  version in the manga there were TV  screens inside this I'm showing him  everything that had been happening and  it's why in response he sent no moves to  store the heroes out of nowhere a giant  whale with a similar Quirk to gang  Walker then burst out of the ground and  inside his mouth is another nomu that  has muscly tentacle arms with drills on  the end these two are said to destroy  the fake Dr garaki presumably so that  the heroes don't capture him and before  the Clone melts away he makes the  observation that Erasure wasn't able to  destroy the double ordinarily you might  expect that because isawa can erase  quirks he should be able to erase a  clone but in reality it just treats the  Clones like actual people following that  more mid-level nomu burst out into the  hospital Reception Area while at the  same time Mirko Rampages through the  morgue this brief clip where she  decapitates The Gnome who really helps  bring to life just how unbelievably fast  and Powerful she is and while that's  going on the real garaki was reluctantly  making plans to run away the reason I  say it's reluctant is because the  doctor's secret lab is basically his  life's work and if he abandons it he  knows that the heroes will likely  destroy everything on the walls you  literally have thousands of quarks  stored in each of these jars and it goes  without saying that these must have been  harvested from innocent people over a  super long period of time in addition to  that there are also multiple higher  gnomus recovering in their tanks so From  garaki's perspective he doesn't want to  leave all that behind that being said he  ultimately doesn't have a choice but to  save just himself in shigaraki and in  order to escape he needs to use the  warping Quirk this Quirk is possessed by  both all for one and Johnny the nomu and  it's the only way the doctor can leave  without having to go through the heroes  however just as he gives Johnny the  order to teleport them away Mirko breaks  down this huge Metal tour with a single  kick shattering hundreds of quirks and  crushing Johnny in the process the  episode then comes to an end with her  asking Dr garaki if he's the real  version and overall I'd personally give  this episode a 9 out of 10. it was great  to start the season by just getting  straight into the main plot rather than  having a filler episode like we usually  do and it had a lot of suspense a lot of  excitement several moments that were  done a lot better than they looked on  paper including the moment when graki  melted away and the moment when twice  was talking about sanctum so yeah  overall I think it was really great  definitely an improvement on the things  we were seeing in season five anyway  that's pretty much everything I wanted  to say about the season premiere but let  me know in the comments what you thought  of the episode and also if you want to  see more breakdowns like this right now  I'm not sure whether I want to do full  episode breakdowns or if I want to do  just videos explaining certain things in  the episode it would be good to get your  guys opinion on that so that I know what  to do going forward and uh yeah until  the next one peace out

